{
  "id": "arcduo",
  "name": "ArcDuo",
  "_comment": [
    "Physical layout for keymap-drawer only; ZMK never reads this file. The",
    "authoritative layout is the zmk,physical-layout node in",
    "boards/shields/arcduo/arcduo.dtsi.",
    "",
    "The two row-4 entries are not keys: they are the integrated trackballs,",
    "placed in the split gap at the inner edge of each half, where they sit on",
    "the case. They exist so the diagram can show what each ball does per",
    "layer, and are matched by the two #ifdef KEYMAP_DRAWER bindings at the end",
    "of every layer in config/arcduo.keymap -- keymap-drawer requires the key",
    "count of each layer to equal the key count of the layout. row/col are",
    "decorative here; keymap-drawer only reads x, y, w, h, r, rx, ry.",
    "",
    "The halves are mirror images of each other about x = 7, balls included.",
    "The gap between them is 4u rather than the 3u this file used before the",
    "balls existed, purely so both balls fit side by side without touching; a",
    "split keyboard's halves sit wherever you put them, so the gap in a diagram",
    "is a drawing choice, not a measurement."
  ],
